      },
      "displayName": "Joshua Allan Westgard",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Abfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I will need clarification on the difference between this and FCREPO-2166.  The current dataset (when all the relationships are correctly built) includes a patent (pcdm:Object) and a single PDF (pcdm:File) for each patent.  These are related objects, but I'm unclear on the intended difference between cross-object relationship and nesting.  Is the idea to have direct containment?  If that is what is meant by nesting we may need to add some different data for that.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
